<title>USA: USDA's Glickman sees Jan release for CRP rules.</title>
<headline>USDA's Glickman sees Jan release for CRP rules.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman Tuesday said he expects the department to unveil its final rules for the Conservation Reserve Program in January and did not forsee &quot;drastic&quot; changes in acreage.</p>
<p>&quot;The goal is to get a final rule out sometime next month,&quot; Glickman said in an interview. He said he and other USDA officials were meeting on the issue later Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I suspect there will be some revisions from the proposed rule...I dont believe you're going to see any radical massive redistribution,&quot; of acreage eligible for the program, Glickman said.</p>
</text>
